<p>An English native, Juliet moved from London to Berlin in 2001. She has a BA (First) in Spanish / Media and Communications (from <a href="http://www.leeds.ac.uk/">the University of Leeds</a>), as well as an MSc in Development Studies (<a href="http://www.soas.ac.uk/">School of Oriental and African Studies</a>, London). During and following her studies, she taught English for the British Council in Paraguay and Brazil. Later, working at <a href="https://www.canninghouse.org/">the Hispanic and Luso-Brazilian Council</a> in London and then at the <a href="http://www.bbc.co.uk/worldserviceradio">BBC World Service</a>, she turned her attention to copywriting, marketing and web design.  Since moving to Berlin, she has translated texts into English from German, Italian, Portuguese, French and Spanish in the areas of science and technology, business and tourism, media, interior design and education.
